### host type mx
host -t mx example.com
--- out
example.com mail is handled by 10 mail.example.com.
example.com mail is handled by 20 backup.example.com.

### host type ns
host -t NS example.com
--- out
example.com name server ns1.example.com.
example.com name server ns2.example.com.

### host type txt
host -t txt example.com
--- out
example.com descriptive text "v=spf1 -all"

### host type soa
host -t soa example.com
--- out
example.com has SOA record ns1.example.com. hostmaster.example.com. 2026102901 7200 3600 1209600 300

### host type srv
host -t srv _ldap._tcp.example.com
--- out
_ldap._tcp.example.com has SRV record 0 5 389 ldap.example.com.

### host type aaaa none
host -t aaaa mail.example.com
--- out
mail.example.com has no AAAA record

